Defers compose across nested calls
==================================

`defer` is function-scoped: every queued defer fires at the
enclosing function's exit, in LIFO order, before control
returns to the caller. When a function `outer` calls
`inner`, `inner`'s defers fire at `inner`'s exit — before
`outer` resumes — and `outer`'s defers fire at `outer`'s
exit, after `inner` has fully returned (including after
its defers ran).

This file pins the composition across the call boundary:

  - `inner` defers complete before control returns to
    `outer`, so traces look like `<inner-body><inner-defer>`
    by the time `outer` resumes.
  - `outer`'s defers fire after the call to `inner`
    finishes (and after `inner`'s defers ran).
  - Multiple defers compose LIFO **within** each frame, but
    do not interleave across frames.

All helpers here return `unit` to dodge the TRISC defer-
with-value-return bug (see
feedback_sysl_trisc_defer_nonunit_return.md). Trace strings
are accumulated through a pointer-to-struct.

    module sysl.tests.lang_features

    struct DncTrace
        s: string

`inner` defers fire before `outer` resumes
------------------------------------------

`inner` writes "I" to the trace and queues a defer that
writes "i". The defer fires at `inner`'s exit, so by the
time `outer` resumes after the call, the trace reads "Ii".
`outer` then writes "O", giving final "IiO".

    dnc_inner_one(t: *DncTrace) -> unit
        defer t.s = t.s + "i"
        t.s = t.s + "I"

    dnc_outer_one(t: *DncTrace) -> unit
        dnc_inner_one(t)
        t.s = t.s + "O"

    #test
    test_inner_defers_complete_before_outer_resumes() -> unit
        var t = DncTrace("")
        dnc_outer_one(&t)
        assert(t.s == "IiO", s"expected 'IiO', got '${t.s}'")

`outer`'s defers fire after `inner` is fully gone
-------------------------------------------------

`outer` has its own defer (writes "o") plus a call to
`inner`. Sequence:

  1. `outer` queues "o".
  2. `outer` calls `inner` which writes "I" and queues "i".
  3. `inner` exits, firing "i". Trace = "Ii".
  4. `outer` writes "O". Trace = "IiO".
  5. `outer` exits, firing "o". Trace = "IiOo".

    dnc_outer_with_own_defer(t: *DncTrace) -> unit
        defer t.s = t.s + "o"
        dnc_inner_one(t)
        t.s = t.s + "O"

    #test
    test_outer_defer_fires_after_inner_fully_returns() -> unit
        var t = DncTrace("")
        dnc_outer_with_own_defer(&t)
        assert(t.s == "IiOo", s"expected 'IiOo', got '${t.s}'")

LIFO within each frame, no interleave
-------------------------------------

Two defers in `inner` ("i2", "i1") and two in `outer`
("o2", "o1"). Each frame fires its defers in LIFO order
**at its own exit**; the two frames don't interleave.
Sequence:

  1. `outer` queues "o1".
  2. `outer` writes "O-pre".
  3. `outer` queues "o2".
  4. `outer` calls `inner`.
  5. `inner` queues "i1".
  6. `inner` writes "I-pre".
  7. `inner` queues "i2".
  8. `inner` writes "I-post".
  9. `inner` exits, firing "i2" then "i1".
 10. `outer` writes "O-post".
 11. `outer` exits, firing "o2" then "o1".

Final trace: "O-preI-preI-posti2i1O-posto2o1".

    dnc_inner_two(t: *DncTrace) -> unit
        defer t.s = t.s + "i1"
        t.s = t.s + "I-pre"
        defer t.s = t.s + "i2"
        t.s = t.s + "I-post"

    dnc_outer_two(t: *DncTrace) -> unit
        defer t.s = t.s + "o1"
        t.s = t.s + "O-pre"
        defer t.s = t.s + "o2"
        dnc_inner_two(t)
        t.s = t.s + "O-post"

    #test
    test_two_defers_per_frame_no_interleave() -> unit
        var t = DncTrace("")
        dnc_outer_two(&t)
        assert(t.s == "O-preI-preI-posti2i1O-posto2o1",
               s"expected 'O-preI-preI-posti2i1O-posto2o1', got '${t.s}'")

Three-deep nesting
------------------

A → B → C with one defer in each frame. Sequence:

  1. A writes "A-pre".
  2. A queues "a".
  3. A calls B.
  4. B writes "B-pre".
  5. B queues "b".
  6. B calls C.
  7. C writes "C".
  8. C queues "c".
  9. C exits, firing "c". Trace = "A-preB-preCc".
 10. B writes "B-post". Trace = "A-preB-preCcB-post".
 11. B exits, firing "b". Trace = "A-preB-preCcB-postb".
 12. A writes "A-post". Trace = "A-preB-preCcB-postbA-post".
 13. A exits, firing "a". Trace = "A-preB-preCcB-postbA-posta".

    dnc_c(t: *DncTrace) -> unit
        t.s = t.s + "C"
        defer t.s = t.s + "c"

    dnc_b(t: *DncTrace) -> unit
        t.s = t.s + "B-pre"
        defer t.s = t.s + "b"
        dnc_c(t)
        t.s = t.s + "B-post"

    dnc_a(t: *DncTrace) -> unit
        t.s = t.s + "A-pre"
        defer t.s = t.s + "a"
        dnc_b(t)
        t.s = t.s + "A-post"

    #test
    test_three_deep_nested_defers() -> unit
        var t = DncTrace("")
        dnc_a(&t)
        assert(t.s == "A-preB-preCcB-postbA-posta",
               s"expected 'A-preB-preCcB-postbA-posta', got '${t.s}'")
